          "def-abs-value",
          "def-integer-power",
          "def-series",
          "thm-geometric-series"
        ],
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#1 (the sign alphabet X={-1,+1}^Z, the shift, and the ball B_R of bounded bilateral sequences)",
        "design_state": "completed-local-definition",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "X := {-1,+1}^Z with the coordinate map phi(sigma)_k=(sigma_k+1)/2 onto the published two-symbol bilateral shift space; the metric D := d(phi(sigma),phi(tau)) with the explicit series D(sigma,tau)=sum 2^{-(|k|+1)}|sigma_k-tau_k|; the shift S(sigma)_k=sigma_{k+1}; the space l-infinity(Z) of bounded bilateral real sequences with the supremum norm and its closed balls B_R. No claim that D is a metric is made here (the companion lemmas prove it and its consequences).",
        "strategy": "Define the listed objects over the published two-symbol shift space and its metric; state exactly which properties are deferred to the companion items.",
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems, AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140 (author's preliminary online edition, complete PDF)",
              "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-ode/ode.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "P. Cvitanovic, R. Artuso, R. Mainieri, G. Tanner, G. Vattay, Chaos: Classical and Quantum (ChaosBook.org, edition 17.6.8, complete PDF)",
              "url": "https://chaosbook.org/chapters/ChaosBook.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "R. Devaney and Z. Nitecki, Shift automorphisms in the Henon mapping, Communications in Mathematical Physics 67 (1979) 137-146",
