        ],
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#1 (the homeomorphism h, invariance, and transfer of the shift's chaos properties)",
        "design_state": "completed-local-argument",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "With F(x,y)=(y,y^2-a-x) and h the coding map, Lambda=h(X) is invariant (F(Lambda)=Lambda) and h is a continuous bijection of X onto Lambda satisfying F o h = h o S; h is a homeomorphism once the Axiom of Countable Choice is granted (used once, through sequential closedness in R^2), Lambda is sequentially compact and compact under AC_omega+DC, and F restricted to Lambda is chaotic in the stated sense (continuous, topologically mixing, dense periodic points, sensitive with constant 2L in the Euclidean metric).",
        "strategy": "Translate the recurrence into the phase map, use closedness of the coding map under sequential compactness for the inverse, transfer mixing and periodic density through the conjugacy, and exhibit sensitivity by flipping a far symbol so that the sign separation 2L appears in the observed coordinate.",
        "sources": {
          "references": [
