      {
        "id": "lem-finite-word-deviations-give-homoclinic-orbits",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Constant codes give the hyperbolic fixed points, and finite nonconstant word codes give distinct homoclinic orbits converging to a fixed point at both ends",
        "dependency_level": 7,
        "deps": [
          "def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space",
          "lem-coded-quadratic-recurrence-is-a-contraction",
          "lem-symbol-locality-gives-coding-continuity",
          "thm-henon-coded-invariant-set-is-conjugate-to-shift",
          "def-stable-unstable-cones-and-line-slopes",
          "def-metric-convergence",
          "def-metric-space",
          "def-continuity-real",
          "thm-of-square-roots",
          "def-abs-value",
          "lem-of-abs-value",
          "thm-geometric-series",
          "lem-geometric-sequence-null"
        ],
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#1 (constant codes, finite-word deviations and their homoclinic limits)",
        "design_state": "completed-local-argument",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "For a>=100 with F and h as before: a constant code sigma_n=s gives the constant sequence x_n=r_s with r_s=1+s sqrt(a+1), hence the fixed point (r_s,r_s); for a code differing from a constant sequence in finitely many coordinates, the coded orbit z_n=F^n h(sigma) satisfies z_n -> (r_s,r_s) as n->+infinity and as n->-infinity, and z_n is never equal to (r_s,r_s) if the code is not constant; in particular finite nonempty word deviations give homoclinic orbits of the fixed points.",
        "strategy": "Constant codes are fixed by the sign-preserving square-root recurrence; the finite-word deviation has constant tails, and the locality estimate forces convergence of the coded orbit to the corresponding constant fixed point in both time directions.",
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-bilateral-symbol-and-bounded-sequence-space": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-coded-quadratic-recurrence-is-a-contraction": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-symbol-locality-gives-coding-continuity": "mathematical-premise",
