        "design_state": "completed-local-definition",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "For F(x,y)=(y,y^2-a-x) and k in (0,1): the cones C^u_k={|u|<=k|v|} and C^s_k={|v|<=k|u|}, the matrices DF(x,y) and DF^{-1}(x,y), the line-slope parametrisations u=hv and v=ru with their graph transforms h->1/(2y-h) and r->1/(2y-r); and, for a bijection G of a metric space with fixed point zbar, the definitions of the stable set W^s(zbar), the unstable set W^u(zbar), homoclinic points, and transverse homoclinic points (two C^1 curves through the point, contained in the stable and unstable sets, with distinct tangent lines).",
        "strategy": "Define the listed geometric objects of the quadratic family and the dynamical-set vocabulary used by the transversality theorem; assert no existence or convergence result.",
