        "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#2 (cone mapping, expansion by lambda=2L-k, contraction lambda^{-2} of the slope maps)",
        "design_state": "completed-local-argument",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Let s be a real bilateral sequence with |s_n|>=L for all n and L>=2, and let k=1/2. Then DF(s_{n-1},s_n) maps C^u_k into itself and expands every vector of C^u_k by at least lambda=2L-k>1; DF^{-1}(s_{n-1},s_n) maps C^s_k into itself with the same expansion. The forward slope maps h->1/(2s_n-h) and the backward slope maps r->1/(2s_n-r) are contractions of [-k,k] with factor lambda^{-2}; the composition over m past (respectively future) coordinates converges uniformly to the unique unstable slope h_n (respectively stable slope r_n), and the resulting lines are invariant under DF.",
        "strategy": "Two-matrix computation on the cones with the lower bound 2L-k, the mean-value form of the slope maps, geometric convergence of the compositions, and uniqueness of the limit.",
