        "statement": "Fix theta in (0,1), c>0 with q=c(theta+theta^{-1})<1, a closed interval J, a two-sign sequence s and a C^2 update M_s:JxJ->J with |partial_i M_s|<=c; for any reference half-orbit y satisfying the recurrence and any boundary value b with |b-y_{-1}|<=(1-q)rho/c there is a unique half-orbit x(b) with x_{-1}=b, x_n=M_{s_n}(x_{n-1},x_{n+1}), within the weighted ball of radius rho/(1-q) about y; the map b->x(b) is C^1 in the weighted supremum norm, its derivative d solves the linearised recurrence with d_{-1}=1, and |d_n|<=|d_0| theta^n with |d_0|<=c/(1-c theta). In particular the curve b->(b,x_0(b)) is a C^1 curve whose tangent (1,d_0) has slope bounded by c/(1-c theta).",
