        "statement": "Let a>=100 and let G=(A,B) be a C^2 diffeomorphism onto its image on an open neighbourhood of [-R-1,R+1]^2 (R=sqrt(a)+3) satisfying the six componentwise closeness inequalities with constant epsilon on that square, where epsilon<=1/6 and eta=C(a,R)epsilon meets the root bounds of the perturbed-recurrence lemma, and assume in addition that the conjugate map S o G^{-1} o S is defined and C^2 on a neighbourhood of the square and satisfies the same six inequalities with the same epsilon. Then the coded set Lambda_G=h_G(X) of the scalar recurrence q_n=M_{sigma_n}(q_{n-1},q_{n+1}) is sequentially compact (compact under AC_omega+DC) and invariant under G, h_G(sigma)=(q_0,V(q_0,q_1)) is a homeomorphism onto Lambda_G (using AC_omega once for the closed-map step) conjugating G to the shift, G restricted to Lambda_G is chaotic in the stated sense with sensitivity constant 2l, the two constant codes give hyperbolic fixed points, and finite nonconstant word codes give transverse homoclinic points of those fixed points.",
        "strategy": "Contraction of the perturbed recurrence with factor 2d<1, finite-locality of the coding map and sign separation for sensitivity, the weighted half-tail lemma for the C^1 curves, the slope bound |d_0|<=2/3 for tangents in complementary cones, and hyperbolicity from closeness of the differential to DF at the constant codes.",
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems, AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140 (author's preliminary online edition, complete PDF)",
