        "reference": "mechanical-horseshoe.md#5 (the smooth P-periodic beta_delta, the Hamiltonian H_delta and its period map)",
        "design_state": "completed-local-definition",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Fix a normalized cutoff w in C_c-infinity((0,1)) with w>=0 and integral 1, a parameter a>=100 and delta>0, P=pi/2+delta. Define the P-periodic beta_delta, equal to zero on [0,pi/2] and to delta^{-1}w((t-pi/2)/delta) on [pi/2,P]; the Hamiltonian H_delta(t,q,p)=(p^2+q^2)/2+beta_delta(t)(a q-q^3/3); the Hamiltonian equations q'=p, p'=-q+beta_delta(t)(q^2-a); the free rotation R(q,p)=(p,-q); the pulse endpoint maps K_delta with the rescaled equations q_s=delta p, p_s=-delta q+w(s)(q^2-a); and the stroboscopic map G_delta=K_delta o R, defined where the solution exists through one period. No regularity or approximation claim is asserted here.",
        "strategy": "Define the periodic field, its flow data and the two endpoint maps over the published stroboscopic-map definition, leaving existence, smoothness and closeness to the companion lemmas.",
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "G. Teschl, Ordinary Differential Equations and Dynamical Systems, AMS Graduate Studies in Mathematics 140 (author's preliminary online edition, complete PDF)",
              "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-ode/ode.pdf"
