        "statement": "On a fixed compact input square containing [-R-1,R+1]^2 (R=sqrt(a)+3): for every sufficiently small delta>0 the rescaled pulse solutions exist on [0,1], the endpoint map K_delta is C-infinity there with K_delta -> K in C^1 as delta->0, where K(q,p)=(q,p+q^2-a) is the delta=0 endpoint map; consequently G_delta=K_delta o R is C-infinity on a neighbourhood of the square, is a diffeomorphism onto its image, is symplectic, and G_delta -> F=K o R in C^1 with explicit O(delta) bounds on the square.",
