        "design_state": "completed-local-example",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "The code sigma with sigma_0=-1 and sigma_n=+1 for n≠0 is not periodic and its coded orbit z_n=F^n h(sigma) converges to (r+,r+) as n->+infinity and as n->-infinity, while z_n≠(r+,r+); more generally, any code differing from a constant sequence in a finite nonempty set of coordinates has the same two-sided convergence and is not a fixed point.",
